# Fabric's own git integration writes every item's definition files (pipeline
# JSON, notebook code, SQL Database objects) with LF line endings. Force LF
# here too, regardless of a clone's core.autocrlf setting, so a local Windows
# commit and a Fabric portal commit never disagree about line endings and
# produce a "whole file changed" diff when nothing textually changed.
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf
